<title>UK: HORSE RACING-CHAMPION STAKES RESULT.</title>
<headline>HORSE RACING-CHAMPION STAKES RESULT.</headline>
<dateline>NEWMARKET, England 1996-10-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Result of the group</p>
<p>one Champion Stakes for three-year-olds and upwards, run over</p>
<p>one and a quarter miles (2 kms) on Saturday:</p>
<p>1. Bosra Sham (ridden by Pat Eddery) 9-4  </p>
<p>2. Halling (Frankie Dettori) evens favourite  </p>
<p>3. Timarida (Johnny Murtagh) 15-2</p>
<p>Six ran</p>
<p>Distances: two and a half lengths, one length.</p>
<p>Winner owned by Wafic Said and trained in England by Henry</p>
<p>Cecil.</p>
<p>Value to winning owner: 174,126 sterling ($276,400)</p>
